<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Gera</h1><p class="st-meta">1835 CE – 1887 CE (approx.) · capital Chala</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The southernmost Gibe Oromo kingdom, remembered for holding the Italian explorers Cecchi and Chiarini captive in 1879 to 1880.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gera emerged as a monarchy around 1835 in the forested highlands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibe-river">Gibe</a>, bordering the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaffa">Kingdom of Kaffa</a>. Like the other Gibe states it was formed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> settlers adopted hereditary kingship and settled government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gera's kings ruled from Chala through officials, with an economy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, honey, civet and slaves traded north to the markets of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-jimma">Kingdom of Jimma</a>. The ruling family adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. In 1879 the court seized the Italian explorers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-cecchi">Antonio Cecchi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-chiarini">Giovanni Chiarini</a>, who was held there until his death; Cecchi was freed in 1880 after Ethiopian intervention.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1887 Gera was conquered by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> and annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-gera.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Gera" width="320" height="289"><figcaption>Image: LeGabrie · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gibe_kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1835 CE – 1887 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oromo</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gera</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1861&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gera" aria-label="Kingdom of Gera on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5683 1891 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Gera lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6003 2147L6029 1964"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6029 1964h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6003 2147h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6003 2147h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1861&amp;focus=kingdom-of-gera">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

